# Cursor IDE Rules for Test Monorepo

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for all code
- Follow functional programming patterns where possible
- Prefer const over let
- Use async/await over promises
- Keep functions small and focused

## File Organization
- Place shared code in packages/shared
- Keep API routes in packages/api/src/routes
- Place React components in packages/web/src/components
- Write E2E tests in packages/e2e/tests

## Naming Conventions
- Use camelCase for variables and functions
- Use PascalCase for components and classes
- Use kebab-case for file names
- Use UPPER_CASE for constants

## Testing
- Write unit tests alongside source files
- E2E tests should cover critical user flows
- Aim for 80%+ code coverage

## Git Practices
- Write meaningful commit messages
- Use conventional commits format
- Keep PRs focused and small
- Always run tests before committing
